fix: settings card enables Stop for launcher-recorded adopted servers

The 0.1.9 runtime could already close launcher-started servers (PID-record
match), but the Settings card disabled its Stop button whenever
`status.spawned` was false — which is exactly the launcher-server case — so
"close all webui" still appeared broken.

- status now reports `stoppable` (spawned, or adopted with a matching
  launcher PID record); the card enables Stop on that instead of `spawned`
- the adopted line distinguishes "launcher-started, can be stopped" from a
  genuinely foreign server
